  {
    "id" : "CloneWithoutCloneable",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce clone() Method Only If Class Implements Cloneable",
    "description" : "Ensures that the clone() method is declared only in classes that implement the Cloneable interface.",
    "explanation" : "*Since CodeNarc 0.19*\n\nThe method clone() should only be declared if the class implements the\nCloneable interface.\n\nNOTE: This is a [CodeNarc Enhanced Classpath\nRule](./codenarc-enhanced-classpath-rules.html). It requires\n**CodeNarc** to have the application classes being analyzed, as well as\nany referenced classes, on the classpath.\n\nExample of violations:\n\n        class ValueClass {\n            ValueClass clone() {\n            }\n        }",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "compilerPhase",
        "default" : "4",
        "description" : "compilerPhase"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
