    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Empty Synchronized Statements",
    "description" : "Detects and prevents empty synchronized blocks that serve no purpose and can confuse readers.",
    "explanation" : "~\n\nChecks for empty *synchronized* statements. Empty *synchronized*\nstatements are confusing and serve no purpose.\n\nHere is an example of code that produces a violation:\n\n        class MyClass {\n            def myMethod() {\n                synchronized(lock) {\n                }\n            }\n        }",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
