    "description" : "Detects when an exception is thrown from a finally block, which can obscure the original exception and cause confusion.",
    "explanation" : "Checks for throwing an exception from within a *finally* block. Throwing\nan exception from a *finally* block is confusing and can hide the\noriginal exception.\n\nHere is an example of code that produces a violation:\n\n        int myMethod() {\n            try {\n                doSomething()\n                throw new Exception()\n            } finally {\n                println 'finally'\n                throw new Exception()   // violation\n            }\n        }",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
